<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to September 18 as released by the Bank of Japan on Thursday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.35 (0.35)	 one year     0.42 (0.43)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.66 (0.68)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.37 (0.37)	 three years  1.21 (1.23)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.38 (0.39)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.60 (0.63)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.32 (0.33)	 three years  1.17 (1.18)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.33 (0.34)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.55 (0.57)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.27 (0.28)	 three years  1.12 (1.13)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Sept 17- Sept 20:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.52 (0.49)   120-150 days  0.50 (UNQ )</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.54 (0.53)   150-180 days  0.57 (0.57)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.53 (0.53)   180-360 days  0.56 (0.60)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.53 (0.52)   over 360 days UNQ  (UNQ )</p>
